# Rule index

The linked checks enforce these rules.
The paragraphs of `AGENTS.md` state the rules marked "Prose only".
`test-kit.md` in the pinned contract gives scenario syntax and spec IDs.

| Rule | Enforced by |
|---|---|
| Each running command executes in a scenario | [Kit executed calls][calls] |
| Call only through `ncly`, `ncly-{{ slug }}`, `exits`, `signal`, or `refuses` | [Kit call forms][links] |
| Each manifest example runs | [Kit examples][examples] |
| Declare each own error and warning code, with its commands and modes | [`extension.Check`][declarations] |
| Observe each declared code in its scope, or supply an `untested` reason with an issue | [Kit code coverage][codes] |
| A dry run and run refuse the same preparation failure on the same input | [Kit `refuses`][refuses] |
| A signal case checks the exit, answer, and surviving files | [Kit `signal`][signal] |
| Template and SDK versions move together through `just update` | [Kit version link][links] |
| The skill names only declared commands | [Kit skill links][links] |
| Sign off through `just signoff` and release through `just release vX.Y.Z` | [Signoff receipt][signoff], [release receipt][release] |
| A copied recipe holds no script | [Core template test][template-test] |
| `acceptance.sh` compares the primary output, from a reader that is not the wrapped program, with an independent reference | Prose only; [release runs acceptance][release] |
| A test claims each line of Failures and Acceptance in `spec.md` | [Kit spec IDs][spec] |
| One bounded job, no arbitrary argument relay; the skill teaches when | Prose only |
| Round 1 records the intake, then the spec, then a failing scenario, then the handler | [Finish gate][finish] checks their commits in the [ledger][ledger] |
| Build each command with the `nicely-extension` skill, in rounds from its first pull request | Prose only |
| The first round writes every line of `spec.md`; a line without a test stays `open` | Prose only |
| Each round ends with an independent review and the readiness review | [Signoff][signoff] runs the [finish gate][finish], which needs a readiness review of the signed commit by a named reviewer |
| At the exit, filled forms, no open line, accepted limits, and a passing readiness verdict for this commit, by a named reviewer, from its findings | [Finish gate][finish] |
| A build has at most 5 rounds | The [ledger][ledger] counts them, and the [finish gate][finish] fails after 5 |
| At the limit, stop and report; an answer that lets the agent choose starts no round | Prose only |
| A pull request for review, a stop report, and the delivery are three acts; deliver only after "Done when" | [Signoff][signoff] runs the [finish gate][finish], and [release][release] needs a receipt with `just finish` |
| The ledger names the head, the reviewers, the commits that each review covered, and the result of `just finish` of each round | [Ledger][ledger] |
| Each finding keeps its ID and its highest severity, and gets a state each round; a `warn` or `block` closes only as `fixed` or `limit` | [Ledger findings][ledger-findings] |
| A change of `spec.md` that narrows a promise to close a `warn` or `block` is a limit that only the user accepts | Prose only |
| A command that replaces a user file proves its invariants with `protect`, `refuses`, `signal`, and `appears` | [Kit `refuses`][refuses], [kit `signal`][signal], [kit `appears`][appears] |

